  "changes": [
    "Derived from @fullcalendar/react 7.1.3: the calendar component, its plugins (day grid, time grid, interaction, list, multi-month), themes, locales and APIs.",
    "Dates and named time zones come from vfull-ui-headless-calendar, so no temporal-polyfill is needed and its fixes apply to the calendar: correct offsets where the polyfill misses paired changes (Casablanca during Ramadan), years 0-99, offsets never printed with \":60\" and local-time milliseconds.",
    "The JSON feed request is vfullcalendar-core's instead of a bundled copy, so a feed URL with a #fragment keeps its range parameters; JsonRequestError is the same class core exports.",
    "The unused temporal-polyfill peer is removed.",
    "setDates no longer clears an existing allDay boolean when options.allDay is omitted or undefined; explicit true/false conversions remain supported."
  ],
  "implementation": {
    "kind": "upstream-fork",
    "replacementStatus": "independent implementation pending",
    "targetScope": "Mounted calendar, date navigation, month and week views, event display, selection and editing."
  },
  "verification": {
    "application": "Four app-shaped mounted checks on Node 24/Bun cover navigation, month/week/day views, custom content, clicks, selection, edit payloads, filtering/unmount and the original/VPM allDay regression. TypeScript 7 verifies v7 callback types and that updateSize is absent.",
    "migration": "The actual application still pins v6.1.17. Its imports, callback/ref types, explicit theme/CSS and sizing call need migration. The full application, pointer drag/resize and its custom CSS are not certified by the jsdom caller probe."
  }
}
